<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kotte</h1><p class="st-meta">1412 CE – 1597 CE · capital Kotte</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Sinhalese kingdom to unite all of Sri Lanka, under Parakramabahu VI, before its kings became clients of the Portuguese.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-vi">Parakramabahu VI</a> took power in 1412 after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alagakkonara-family">Alakeshvara</a> family of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gampola">Kingdom of Gampola</a>, possibly with Chinese backing following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He's</a> intervention. He moved the capital to the fortified town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombo">Colombo</a>, which the Alakeshvaras had built as a defence against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jaffna-kingdom">Jaffna Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-vi">Parakramabahu VI</a> reigned for over five decades and briefly unified the island, conquering the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jaffna-kingdom">Jaffna Kingdom</a> and subduing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vanni-chieftaincies">Vanni chieftaincies</a>. His reign was a golden age of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinhala-language">Sinhala</a> poetry, with the monk-poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thotagamuwe-sri-rahula-thera">Sri Rahula</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a> controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinnamon">cinnamon</a>-growing west coast, whose trade attracted the Portuguese, who arrived in 1505 and soon built a fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombo">Colombo</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1521 the kingdom split into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-jayawardenepura-kotte">Kotte</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-sitawaka">Kingdom of Sitawaka</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-raigama">Kingdom of Raigama</a>. Kotte's king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharmapala-of-kotte">Dharmapala</a> converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and in 1580 bequeathed his realm to the King of Portugal; on his death in 1597 it became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-ceylon">Portuguese Ceylon</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kotte.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kotte" width="320" height="229"><figcaption>Image: Blackknight12 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kotte.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1412 CE – 1597 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kotte</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Parakramabahu VI, Bhuvanaikabahu VII, Dharmapala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sinhala</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kotte, Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1504&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kotte" aria-label="Kingdom of Kotte on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6892 1920 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kotte lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7212 2176L7211 2175M7212 2176L7230 2166M7212 2176L4773 1044M7212 2176L7208 2073M7212 2176L7230 2166M7212 2176L7231 2161"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7211 2175h0M7230 2166h0M4773 1044h0M7208 2073h0M7230 2166h0M7231 2161h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7212 2176h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7212 2176h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1504&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kotte">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
